  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 101 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nWidespread showers are expected on Thursday, due to increasing\nmoisture and warm air advection ahead of a strong approaching\ntrough of low pressure. Though confidence is high in precip\nchances overall, there are indications that the higher rainfall\ntotals may be north near toward the better upper trough forcing\nand also south near the surface low track. Overall though, the\nforcing and moisture are enough to maintain high precip chances\nfor the forecast area. \n\nThe main cold front with the late week system is expected to\nmove through Thursday evening, with the trough passage late\nThursday night into early Friday morning. A few showers may\nlinger with the trough passage late Thu into early Fri, but\nprecip chances will be much lower behind the cold front as a\nmuch drier airmass moves in. Much cooler conditions are also\nexpected behind this system, with highs only in the 50s Friday\nand Saturday. It still looks like there is the potential for the\nfirst widespread frost of the season Friday night into Saturday\nmorning under high pressure. \n\nSurface high pressure is expected to be in place across the\nregion much of the time over the weekend into early next week,\nwith dry weather likely through this period. Southerly winds\nwill develop on the back side of the high by early next week,\nwith temperatures returning to at least normal, if not several\ndegrees above normal by Tuesday.\n\nDDV",
